# Context & token discipline

Principle: **the right context, for the right agent, at the right time—in the smallest sufficient amount.**  
Inspired by [jasontang-ai/Context-Engineering](https://github.com/jasontang-ai/Context-Engineering) (MIT) — merged, not vendored. Detail: `ecc-cherry-pick/context-engineering.md`.

## Progressive load

1. Start from: captain request, approved scope / `ACTIVE_TASK.json`, project conventions, `DECISIONS.md` pointers.
2. Discover with search/glob **before** opening whole files.
3. Open only architecture, requirements, design-system, and code slices needed for this task.
4. Expand when correctness, security, dependencies, reuse discovery, or verification require it.
5. Never omit critical constraints (approvals, security, AC) just to stay under a budget.
6. Load `ecc-cherry-pick/ui-craft.md` / `ui-stress.md` **only** for relevant UI work; backend-only and tiny copy patches skip them.

## Soft budgets (guidelines, not hard caps)

| Scale | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| patch | Task + touched files + theme tokens; skip full PRD/DESIGN |
| module | ACTIVE_TASK + relevant DESIGN/REQUIREMENTS sections + feature paths |
| product | Pipeline docs as needed per phase — not the entire history every turn |

## Prune & retrieve

- Prefer relevant over exhaustive; summarize long nonessential tool output.
- Keep exact code/errors/logs when debugging.
- Do not re-scan the repo or re-read unchanged large docs without a reason.
- Load skills/subagents only when needed; one implementer for simple patches.
- Handoffs carry essentials only (see `templates/sdlc/HANDOFF.md`); no scope expansion implied.
- Context cutting must **not** skip reusable-component search or craft standards (`04-code-craft`).

## Models / chat hygiene

- Prefer **Auto**; subagents `model: inherit`; no frontier pins unless captain orders.
- Prefer new chat per phase/module; do not drag full product PRD into a one-line patch.
- Optimize tokens **per correctly verified task**, not shorter answers that skip verification.
